<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fall on improved arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fall on improved arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell sharply by 250-300 rupees per tonne on Monday on increased arrivals at markets and processing plants in central India, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the market undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also down on a higher supply by soybean processing plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent fell 200 rupees and soyoil refined lost 400 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were down on limited demand. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $272 per tonne in ready delivery and at $265-266 per tonne for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was offered at $120-121 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at 4,150 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,100-4,125 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
